# The CloudWatch agent the Bazel cache writer runs (deploy/termag-bazel-cache-writer.user-data.sh
# installs it, refusing anything whose sha256 isn't this one). arm64 Ubuntu package, from the
# agent's us-east-2 bucket, which the writer reaches through the VPC's S3 gateway endpoint.
#
# Where the hash comes from (2026-11-03): AWS's latest at the time
# (https://amazoncloudwatch-agent.s3.amazonaws.com/info/latest/CWAGENT_VERSION), downloaded from
# `url` with its signature `sig_url`. `gpg --verify` said "Good signature from Amazon CloudWatch
# Agent" with the key at https://amazoncloudwatch-agent.s3.amazonaws.com/assets/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.gpg,
# whose fingerprint is the one AWS documents ("Verifying the signature of the CloudWatch agent
# package"): 9376 16F3 450B 7D80 6CBD 9725 D581 6730 3B78 9C72. `dpkg-deb -f` says
# amazon-cloudwatch-agent 1.300074.1b2005-1, arm64. Then sha256sum.
#
# To move it: the same steps for the new version, all three lines together.
version=1.300074.1b2005
url=https://amazoncloudwatch-agent-us-east-2.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/ubuntu/arm64/1.300074.1b2005/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb
sha256_linux_arm64=3af82796de0f5ebe230cf72fa9bbcf9270dda9d03cae72bdcf2bee2abe877b26
